cc/build_engine/build_engine.py (stdlib only, python3) — CLI: `build_engine.py --source DIR --commit SHA [--patch FILE] --tag NAME --out DIR`. Steps: verify source commit/tree via git, copy source to a temp staging dir and apply patch (git apply --check first), run buildx bake with --metadata-file, capture full stdout/stderr to <out>/build.stdout|stderr (ALSO on failure), `docker save` the image to <out>/engine-image.docker.tar and compute sha256+bytes, read image config ID and RepoDigests/Created/Architecture/OS via `docker image inspect`, extract sha256 of /app/llama-bench etc. from the image (docker create/cp or docker run --entrypoint sha256sum), record base image digests, buildx/docker versions, cmake flags, patch sha256 (or null), dirty-tree state, build wall time. Write <out>/build-record.json (all of that + status success|failed + failure_stage) and exit nonzero on failure. Must not use --push, must not mount the docker socket into any image, must not touch other containers or prune anything. Record whether buildx provenance was retained in the saved archive (inspect index.json / attestation manifests) — do NOT claim it if absent.\nassignments/T-D-build-cc.md:9:4. cc/build_engine/README.md — agent-facing instructions: when to use, inputs/outputs, how to add a patch, failure modes, what is NOT proven (no bitwise reproducibility claim).\nassignments/T-D-build-cc.md:10:5. cc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py (pytest, no GPU, no real build): unit tests for patch-check failure path, record schema with a mocked docker runner, and sha256/bytes computation.\nassignments/T-C-llamacpp-compare.md:2:Goal context: we are reverse-engineering the *methodology* behind Strata (MoE expert slots/residency/CPU-GPU dispatch) to decide what tools and components WE must build for something similar. Other engines are inspiration inputs.\nassignments/T-C-llamacpp-compare.md:9: 3. instrumentation-options.md — cheapest ways to log router top-k expert IDs per layer/token from llama.cpp