Git are accepted. Submodules are rejected. Git archive honors committed export attributes; ignored and untracked files and `.git` are omitted. Docker ignore files in the staged snapshot are emptied to prevent omission of tracked source. Temporary staging is removed after either result. Keep the supplied patch and original commit for rebuilding; patch bytes are identified by SHA256 but are not retained as a separate output artifact.\ncc/build_engine/README.md:23:The image contains only the seven requested tools in `/app`, their generated shared libraries and the OpenMP runtime, on top of the CUDA runtime base. It has no compiler, source checkout, or weights. Its entrypoint is cleared, so invoke tools by full path, for example `/app/llama-bench`. Release/shared CUDA compilation uses the flags in `build-record.json`; CPU-native tuning, tests, downloaded UI, and OpenSSL are disabled. `LLAMA_CURL=OFF` is passed as requested, although this checkout treats LLAMA_CURL as deprecated. Source and patch identity are recorded as image labels; binaries' built-in Git version may say `unknown` because `.git` is not staged.\ncc/build_engine/README.md:27:`build-record.json` uses schema version 1. It records status, failure stage/error, requested and resolved commit, Git tree ID and dirty status, patch SHA256 or null, tag/platform, recipe SHA256 and sizes, base references/digests, Docker and Buildx versions, CMake flags, Buildx metadata, image config ID/RepoDigests/Created/Architecture/Os, tool SHA256 values, saved archive SHA256/bytes, build duration and total duration. Fields remain null or empty when a failure occurs before collection. `build_wall_seconds` measures the Bake invocation, including export; `wall_seconds` covers the whole attempt.\ncc/build_engine/README.md:35:The CLI exits 0 only after all evidence collection succeeds, otherwise nonzero. Failures include source mismatch/dirty tree, unsupported submodules, malformed or inapplicable patch, unavailable Docker/base image, build/export failure, incorrect architecture, missing binaries, save failure, or malformed archive. A failure after building can leave the tagged local image and partial evidence; inspect `failure_stage` and retry in a fresh output directory. Invalid CLI arguments, an unwritable output path, or a nonempty output directory fail before a record can be created. Existing evidence is never overwritten. The CLI does not push, prune, mount the Docker socket in an image, or operate on unrelated containers. A single short-lived `docker run --rm --network=none --read-only --entrypoint /usr/bin/sha256sum` container hashes the tools without requesting a GPU. Subsequent hashing and saving use the immutable config ID so a later tag change cannot change the evidence target.\ncc/build_engine/README.md:52:Tests use temporary Git repositories and mocked Docker subprocesses. They cover patch rejection, successful patch isolation, successful record schema, build failure logs/metadata, dirty or mismatched source, archive/tool hashing, provenance versus SBOM, and refusing to overwrite evidence. They use no network, GPU, or real build.\ncc/engine_handoff/example/facts.md:17:- `build_record.claims.patch_sha256` [declared]: null\ncc/engine_handoff/example/facts.md:66:- build_record.patch_sha256: declared (not independently verified)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
